WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.469
-There's a thing that happened
over the weekend in Iowa

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.036
that went viral.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:07.574
A person came up to talk to you,
and it was very --

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.008
it was an emotional moment,

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.743
and I just want to show a clip
of that, if you don't mind.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.045
-Sure.
-Check this out.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:15.147
-Hi. My name is Raelyn.
-Hi, Raelyn.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:18.485
-I was wondering if there was
ever a time in your life

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:21.087
where somebody you really looked
up to, [Voice breaking] um --

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:26.425
maybe didn't accept you as much,
and how you dealt with that.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:31.997
-My mother and I
had very different views...

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:36.369
of how to build a future.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:41.707
[ Voice breaking ] You just
got to do what's right inside

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.910
and...hope that maybe

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.280
the rest of the world
will come around to it.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.916
And maybe they will,
and maybe they won't.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.720
The truth is, you got to
take care of yourself first

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.688
and do this.
Give me a hug.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.957
-Oh. Oh.
[ Applause ]

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.459
-Oh. Oh.

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:02.595
-That was emotional.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.998
That went all over the place.
What made you guys connect?

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:08.000
What made you emotional there?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.404
-You know, I could see her face.
-Aww.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.172
-And as she started
this question,

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:16.508
I knew that she was in
the middle of something tough.

00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:18.877
-Yeah.
-Someone she respected,

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:21.847
who wasn't -- didn't approve
of what she was --

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:25.351
where she was.
And you know, a lot of people

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:28.021
don't know,
I dropped out of school at 19,

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.456
got married to someone my mother
wanted me to marry.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:35.828
And when Raelyn started to speak
it's, like, all of a sudden,

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.930
I was back on the phone
with my mother,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.667
trying to explain
that after these years,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.136
he had walked out
and he wasn't coming back.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.538
-That's tough.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.873
-And I knew how
she would feel about that.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.209
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.044
-Did your mom ever come around?
-[ Sighs ]

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:53.779
You know, we got back
together over it.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:57.116
It was okay, but it is --
sometimes you just got to

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.552
do what's right.
-Yeah, that was great.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:03.122
It's those moments like that,
that they're kind of unexpected,

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:06.526
obviously unplanned, but
you must go to so many campaigns

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.460
and kind of answer
the same questions.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.297
But something like that,
does that re-energize you?

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:15.534
-You know, for me, it's --
I do selfie lines.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:20.440
So, I get that one-on-one,
and you know,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.642
I don't do big-dollar
fundraisers at all.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.809
-Yeah.
-I don't go suck up

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:25.844
to billionaires
and corporate executives.

00:02:25.844 --> 00:02:29.548
I've won my campaign
entirely with people

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:32.918
who pitch in
20 bucks and 5 bucks.

00:02:32.918 --> 00:02:36.022
And I get to call those people.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:40.793
In fact, if anyone goes
to elizabethwarren.com tonight

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:45.431
and pitches in 5 bucks
on the campaign or more,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.768
tomorrow I will make calls
to people to say "Thank you,"

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:51.437
because I think that's
how democracy ought to work.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.772
-Wow. Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.839
-Get right on the phone
and talk to them?

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:54.941
-Oh, yeah.

